    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d440-a1">

                <pb facs="0324" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg252"/>

                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Limerick</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-06">May 6, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>Proposed by Richard Russell, esq., J. P., seconded by Councillor Lyman, J. P.,
                    and unanimously passed:</p>
                <p>That this meeting views with the deepest abhorrence the assassination of the
                    President of the United States, and desire to record their most heartfelt
                    sympathy with the American people in the great national loss sustained by the
                    removal from the head of the government of a man who displayed, in the discharge
                    of his duties, the greatest ability and zeal for the interest of the people over
                    whom he presided.</p>
                <p>Proposed by Caleb Powell, esq., J. P., seconded by Eugene O’Callaghan, esq., J.
                    P., and carried unanimously:</p>
                <pb facs="0325" n="253" xml:id="pg253"/>
                <p>That as Irishmen we feel it our duty to express our deep sorrow and indignation
                    of the attempt to assassinate Mr. Seward, Foreign Secretary of the States of
                    America.</p>
                <p>Proposed by Alderman Quarter an, J. P., and seconded by Thomas Boyse, esq., J.
                    P.:</p>
                <p>That copies of the resolutions now passed be forwarded to the American minister
                    in London, and to Mrs. Lincoln and Mrs. Seward.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN R. TINSLEY,</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mayor of Limerick, Chairman of Meeting</hi>.</closer>
            </div>
